{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyMzYzMA==","is_bot":false,"login":"rparcus","name":"Robert Parcus"},"body":"## Overview\nImplement specialized prisms or beams for processing and transforming Telegram messages, enabling advanced message handling and response generation.\n\n## Core Features\n- Message content analysis\n- Command parsing and routing\n- Message formatting (Markdown, HTML)\n- Message threading support\n- Reply management\n- Deep linking handling\n- Callback query processing\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Complete prism implementations for all message types\n- [ ] Command parser with parameter extraction\n- [ ] Format conversion utilities\n- [ ] Thread management system\n- [ ] Documentation with examples\n- [ ] Test coverage > 90%\n- [ ] Performance optimization\n\n## Budget: $2,000","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc7L00jO","author":{"login":"mudaly10-coder"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Auto-claim: taking this on (HAF).\nWill submit a minimal PR quickly; happy to align scope/acceptance if needed.","createdAt":"2025-10-19T12:16:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-3419621582","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc7s-8kJ","author":{"login":"KimberleyOCaseyfv"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Claim: Telegram Message Processing\n\nHi @Spectral-Finance team,\n\nI'd like to claim this task. I have experience building Telegram bots and message processing systems.\n\n**My approach:**\n1. Analyze existing Lux prism/beam architecture\n2. Design message type prisms (text, photo, callback, etc.)\n3. Implement command parser with parameter extraction\n4. Add message threading and reply management\n5. Create comprehensive tests\n\n**Timeline:** \n- Day 1-2: Architecture review and design\n- Day 3-5: Core prism implementations  \n- Day 6-7: Testing and documentation\n\n**Questions:**\n1. Are there existing Telegram-related utilities in the codebase I should reuse?\n2. Should this support both Bot API and MTProto?\n3. Any specific formatting requirements for Markdown/HTML?\n\nLooking forward to contributing!\n\ncc: @maintainers","createdAt":"2026-02-28T00:57:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-3975923977","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCHJDoA","author":{"login":"Treasure520520"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #63\n\nI am working on a focused Telegram message-processing core for this bounty: update classification, command parsing with args and bot mentions, MarkdownV2/HTML escaping, thread/reply context extraction, deep-link payload parsing, callback query decoding, docs, and focused tests. I will submit a PR shortly.","createdAt":"2026-05-13T02:39:12Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4436673440","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCHPKFQ","author":{"login":"lyons811"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #63\n\nI am working on a scoped Telegram message-processing layer for Lux: pure update classification, command/deep-link parsing, MarkdownV2/HTML formatting, thread/reply/callback context extraction, agent-facing prisms, docs, and unit coverage. I will keep the PR side-effect free and compatible with the existing Telegram send/edit prisms.","createdAt":"2026-05-13T03:02:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4436773397","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCQoMhA","author":{"login":"BigPolarBear"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #63\n\nSubmitted a focused Telegram message-processing implementation: https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/pull/552\n\nScope covers update classification, message type detection, command parsing with args and bot mentions, MarkdownV2/HTML escaping, thread/reply context extraction, deep-link payload parsing, callback query decoding, route suggestions, docs, and unit/integration tests.\n\nBounty wallet: 0x38938CB6Fd54172C5E82a5d01a9236fF12E84BdF","createdAt":"2026-05-14T01:36:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4446620804","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCQyJWA","author":{"login":"CusGroup"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi, I’m interested in taking this bounty.\n\nI have recent hands-on experience with production Telegram/message-processing flows, webhook-style routing, auth/proxy compatibility, and reliability debugging. I can start by reviewing the acceptance criteria, reproducing the current behavior, then delivering a focused PR with tests/verification notes.\n\nProposed approach:\n1. Confirm expected Telegram message flow and edge cases.\n2. Reproduce current failing/missing behavior locally.\n3. Implement processing logic with minimal blast radius.\n4. Add validation/test coverage and clear handoff notes.\n\nIf this bounty is still open, please confirm assignment rules and I’ll begin.","createdAt":"2026-05-14T02:03:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4446783832","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCZkj5Q","author":{"login":"zp6"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'm working on this issue. PR #605 implements the complete Telegram Message Processing pipeline with message analysis, command parsing, format conversion, thread management, reply management with templates, and deep link handling.","createdAt":"2026-05-15T01:10:01Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4455998437","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCaScOA","author":{"login":"laolaoqi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi, I'm interested in the Telegram Message Processing bounty. I have solid experience with message queue architectures and NLP preprocessing.\n\nMy approach:\n- Build a pipeline for receiving and processing Telegram messages via the Lux framework\n- Support text, media, and command message types\n- Message filtering, routing, and transformation modules\n- Configurable handlers for different message patterns\n- Async processing with backpressure handling\n\nI can deliver within 7-10 days after assignment discussion. Let's connect on Discord.\n\nPayment wallet: 0xdFc476D7Bb10230B26500eEE24e300B26d253561","createdAt":"2026-05-15T03:55:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4456750136","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCatQ5g","author":{"login":"laolaoqi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"?? Interested in this Telegram Message Processing (,000) bounty. Experienced with Telegram bot message routing, webhook processing, and async message queues. Can deliver within 2 weeks. Payment: 0xdFc476D7Bb10230B26500eEE24e300B26d253561","createdAt":"2026-05-15T05:37:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4457189606","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABEXnNFA","author":{"login":"MyTH-zyxeon"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Maintainer-facing acceptance synthesis for #63 / PRs #552 and #605.\n\nI am not claiming this bounty or asking maintainers to prefer a specific submitter. This is a review-assist synthesis to make the Telegram Message Processing acceptance surface easier to compare.\n\nVisible implementation surface checked:\n- Issue: #63, \"Telegram Message Processing ($2,000)\"\n- Visible submitted PRs: #552 and #605\n\nWhat each visible attempt appears to cover:\n- #552 is a compact offline update processor under `Lux.Integrations.Telegram.MessageProcessor`, plus a `ProcessUpdate` prism, docs, and focused unit/integration coverage. It emphasizes deterministic offline classification, command parsing, formatting helpers, thread/reply/callback/deep-link handling, and no network calls.\n- #605 is broader and decomposes the work into separate prisms for message analysis, command parsing, format conversion, thread management, reply management, and deep-link handling, plus a processing beam. It has a wider feature surface, but previous review notes identified compile/beam-wiring and dry-run boundary risks that should be resolved before acceptance.\n\nAcceptance checks I would use before marking #63 complete:\n1. Message-type coverage: text, command, callback query, reply, edited message, media-caption, bot mention, and deep-link update shapes should be normalized or explicitly rejected with deterministic errors.\n2. Command parsing contract: `/command`, `/command@bot`, quoted args, positional args, `--key value`, `--key=value`, short flags, boolean flags, and invalid/missing arguments should have documented behavior and tests.\n3. Format conversion safety: Markdown, MarkdownV2, HTML, and plain-text conversions should preserve semantics where possible and test escaping edge cases such as nested entities, links, code blocks, mentions, underscores, and HTML-sensitive characters.\n4. Thread and reply state: thread creation, lookup, reply chaining, lifecycle cleanup, and process-boundary persistence should be explicit. Public ETS or in-memory state should include ownership, cleanup, and concurrency assumptions.\n5. Deep-link and callback routing: payload parsing, referral/campaign extraction, callback data validation, malformed payloads, and handler dispatch should be tested without requiring Telegram network access.\n6. Beam/prism boundary: any auto-reply or response generation path should support a dry-run/planning mode so review can verify what would be sent without sending a Telegram message.\n7. Performance and coverage evidence: the bounty asks for >90% test coverage and performance optimization, so maintainers need either coverage output or an agreed focused test command plus simple bounds for large message batches.\n8. Credential-free validation: acceptance should be reproducible with fixtures only; no bot token, webhook registration, live chat mutation, message send/edit/delete, callback acknowledgement, or media upload should be required.\n\nSuggested merge bar:\n- `mix format`, compile, and the repository's accepted focused Telegram message-processing test command pass on the submitted branch.\n- The selected PR demonstrates message analysis, command parsing, formatting, threading, reply/deep-link/callback behavior, docs, and coverage/performance evidence.\n- The implementation has a clear no-network default path, with any live Telegram side effects behind explicit adapters or dry-run boundaries.\n\nThis should help compare #552, #605, and any later attempts against #63 without requiring maintainers to reconstruct the Telegram processing safety matrix from multiple PR threads.\n","createdAt":"2026-05-31T21:32:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4588162324","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABIvaYpw","author":{"login":"sureshchouksey8"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Implemented in PR #886. The PR now maps the Telegram Message Processing acceptance criteria to concrete parser, formatter, thread-manager, prism, beam, and test files, with validation evidence posted on the PR. Requesting bounty review when convenient.","createdAt":"2026-07-04T10:01:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4881553575","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABI0SE1g","author":{"login":"sureshchouksey8"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Implemented in PR #886. The PR now maps the Telegram Message Processing acceptance criteria to concrete parser, formatter, thread-manager, prism, beam, and test files, with validation evidence posted on the PR. Requesting bounty review when convenient.","createdAt":"2026-07-05T16:02:06Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4886660310","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABI6tGPA","author":{"login":"hyperxiaoerxz-hash"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I read through the Telegram message-processing bounty. I would start with a narrow, testable slice: command parsing with args/bot mentions, MarkdownV2/HTML formatting utilities, callback query handling, and regression tests around Telegram edge cases.\n\nI have a small Telegram automation scanner repo here: https://github.com/hyperxiaoerxz-hash/telegram-bounty-scanner\n\nIf this is still open for contributors, I can take the parser/formatter/callback layer first and keep it reviewable before broader message-threading work.\n","createdAt":"2026-07-06T13:32:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63#issuecomment-4893394492","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2025-02-25T10:10:09Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6PoGQw","name":"bounty","description":"","color":"395808"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"Telegram Message Processing ($2,000)","updatedAt":"2026-07-06T13:32:37Z","url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/63"}
